{{!< default}}
{{!-- One article.

The order of the children of <article> is the sheet's, not a preference: the meta line and
the h1 sit in a <header>, the same facts repeat in an <aside class="post-info"> that only
desktop shows, the table of contents is a sibling rail, and the words live in
`#post-body.prose`.

THE BYLINE IS PRINTED TWICE, and that is the fix rather than the bug. `.post-meta` is hidden
on desktop — the facts move to the right-hand column there — so a byline printed only in the
meta line is invisible on every desktop screen.

TWO THINGS ARE FILLED IN BY SCRIPT, both by `quireink.article()` immediately below the
article body, while the parser is still standing there and before the page is painted:

  · The TABLE OF CONTENTS. Ghost gives headings no ids and a Handlebars template cannot read
    the rendered HTML it just printed, so the rail is built from `#post-body` — ids on the
    h2/h3 by the engine's own slug rule, then the `<nav class="toc rail">` inserted before
    the body. It has to be before first paint: the sheet's three-column layout keys off a
    `.rail` being there, and a rail that arrives late is a page that jumps.
  · The WORD COUNT. Ghost stores reading time and not word count; `{{reading_time}}` is the
    platform's own number and is printed as it comes, but the count beside it is measured
    off the rendered text the way the engine measures it off the source. --}}
<div class="with-rail"><main id="content">

{{#post}}
<article class="{{post_class}}">

{{#if @custom.post_feature_image}}{{#if feature_image}}
{{!-- The picture goes ABOVE the headline, not under it, and it is off unless the owner asks.
Both are the blog engine's calls: a hero under the title pushes the first sentence off a
phone screen, and a default that switched pictures on would redesign every article a site had
already published. --}}
<div class="post-hero"><img src="{{img_url feature_image size="xl"}}" alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{else}}{{title}}{{/if}}" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div>
{{/if}}{{/if}}

<header>
<p class="t-small text-meta post-meta">
    <time datetime="{{date published_at format="YYYY-MM-DD"}}">{{date published_at}}</time>
    &middot; <span class="num" data-word-count></span> words
    &middot; <span class="num">{{reading_time minute="1" minutes="%"}}</span> min read
    {{#primary_author}} &middot; <span class="byline">{{name}}</span>{{/primary_author}}
    <span class="meta-book"> &middot; <button type="button" class="book-mode-toggle" data-book-open>Book mode</button></span>
</p>
<h1 class="reading-font mt-2 fs-h1 font-semibold">{{title}}</h1>
</header>

<aside class="post-info t-small text-meta">
    <p><time datetime="{{date published_at format="YYYY-MM-DD"}}">{{date published_at}}</time></p>
    {{#primary_author}}<p class="byline">{{name}}</p>{{/primary_author}}
    <p><span class="num" data-word-count></span> words</p>
    <p><span class="num">{{reading_time minute="1" minutes="%"}}</span> min read</p>
    {{#if tags}}<p class="info-terms">Tags: <span class="term-list">{{#foreach tags}}<a class="link-accent lower" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/foreach}}</span></p>{{/if}}
    <p class="info-action"><button type="button" class="book-mode-toggle" data-book-open>Book mode</button></p>
</aside>

<div id="post-body" class="prose">{{content}}</div>
<script>quireink.article()</script>

{{#if tags}}
<span class="anchor" id="post-tags"></span>
<hr class="taxo-rule">
<footer class="post-taxo t-small text-meta">
    <p class="info-terms">Tags: <span class="term-list">{{#foreach tags}}<a class="link-accent lower" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/foreach}}</span></p>
</footer>
{{/if}}

{{#prev_post}}
<hr>
<section class="read-next">
    <p class="read-next-label">Read next</p>
    <p class="read-next-title reading-font"><a class="link-accent" href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a></p>
</section>
{{/prev_post}}

{{#if primary_tag}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tags:{{primary_tag.slug}}+id:-{{id}}" limit="3" as |related|}}
    {{#if related}}
    <hr>
    <section class="related">
        <h2>Related posts</h2>
        <ul>
            {{#foreach related}}
            <li>
                <a class="link-accent" href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a>
                <p class="t-small text-meta">{{date published_at}}</p>
            </li>
            {{/foreach}}
        </ul>
    </section>
    {{/if}}
{{/get}}
{{/if}}

</article>

{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
{{!-- The blog engine's sign-up card, at the end of an article. `core.js` intercepts the
submit and posts to `/api/subscribe`; `ghost-bridge.js` turns that into Ghost's own
`send-magic-link`, so the card is real rather than decorative. The header's mail control
opens the same card as an overlay. --}}
<section class="subscribe-card" id="subscribe">
<h2>Subscribe to the newsletter</h2>
<form class="subscribe" method="post" action="/api/subscribe">
<input type="email" name="email" required aria-label="your@email.com" placeholder="your@email.com"><button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
<input class="hp" type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true">
</form>
<p class="subscribe-status" role="status"></p>
</section>
{{/if}}

{{#if @site.comments_enabled}}
{{!-- Ghost's own thread, not the engine's. The engine's comment island mounts on `#comments`
and this deliberately is not that id: Ghost has a comment system with sign-in, replies and
moderation behind it, and a theme that shipped a second one would own the half of it Ghost
already does better. docs/decisions/0004. --}}
<section id="post-comments" class="post-comments">
    {{comments title="Comments" count=false}}
</section>
{{/if}}

{{/post}}

</main></div>
